{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Writhing</b> — Because he mentioned the birth pang of a woman in labor, he said: חולי וגוחי — the child has come out, as in: כי אתה גוחי מבטן." "<b>מקריה</b> — It is Jerusalem and all the towns around it. And the meaning: the settlement." "<b>And you shall dwell in the field</b> — When you go into exile." "<b>And you shall come as far as Babylon</b> — There is the exile of Nebuchadnezzar; there I will redeem you."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase חולי וגוחי combines a noun and verb from the same root; both forms are preserved in Hebrew as Ibn Ezra quotes them."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:54.575452253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}